* FD-13 / FD-14  Small- and large-signal step response, slew rate, settling
* Spec 3.1.4.1, Fig. 32: capacitive gain -1 (input and feedback C = {{C_NET}} F),
* VINP and VINN step by +{{V_HI}} V and -{{V_HI}} V in antiphase.  The capacitors give the
* inputs VP and VN no DC path, so a differential-only servo (the E sources of the FD noise
* bench) sets their DC level through switches: at DC, Vod sits at the amplifier's own offset
* and the input common mode at VCOM (.nodeset only guides the DC solution to that state).  The
* switches open well before the first edge, so during
* the step the network is purely capacitive.  Vod steps by 2*{{V_HI}} V;
* slew rate is the
* largest slope of Vod (SR+, SR-), settling is to +/-0.1 % of the step.
* RSP/RSN: source resistance ({{RS}} ohm, spec section 2).
{{SEED_OPTION}}
.lib "{{MODEL_LIB}}" {{CORNER}}
{{MC_PARAM}}
.include "{{DUT_FILE}}"
.temp {{TEMP}}
.options reltol=1e-6 abstol=1e-15 vntol=1e-9 method=gear
VDD vdd 0 {{VDD}}
VSS vss 0 0
IBIAS vdd ibias {{IBIAS}}
VCM vcm 0 {{VCM}}
VIP vips vcm PULSE(0 {{V_HI}} {{T_DELAY}} {{T_EDGE}} {{T_EDGE}} {{T_WIDTH}} {{T_PERIOD}})
VIN vins vcm PULSE(0 {{V_HI_NEG}} {{T_DELAY}} {{T_EDGE}} {{T_EDGE}} {{T_WIDTH}} {{T_PERIOD}})
RSP vips vip {{RS}}
RSN vins vin {{RS}}
C1 vip inp {{C_NET}}
C2 inp outn {{C_NET}}
C3 vin inn {{C_NET}}
C4 inn outp {{C_NET}}
EP sp vcm outn outp 0.5
EN sn vcm outp outn 0.5
SP sp inp hold 0 servo
SN sn inn hold 0 servo
VHOLD hold 0 PWL(0 1 {0.1*{{T_DELAY}}} 1 {0.2*{{T_DELAY}}} 0)
.model servo sw vt=0.5 vh=0 ron=1 roff=1e15
XDUT vss ibias vdd vcmpin inp inn outp outn {{DUT}}
RVCM_DUT vcm vcmpin 1k
RLP outp vcm {{RL}}
CLP outp 0 {{CL}}
RLN outn vcm {{RL}}
CLN outn 0 {{CL}}
.nodeset v(inp)={{VCM}} v(inn)={{VCM}} v(outp)={{VCM}} v(outn)={{VCM}}
.control
set filetype=ascii
tran {{TSTEP}} {{TSTOP}} 0 {{TMAX}}
write {{RAW}} v(outp) v(outn)
.endc
.end
